fix: never leak handler exceptions into the group; add debug commands

The /shit help failure surfaced as an AstrBot plugin-error traceback
posted into the group. Root causes:

- core/commands.CommandResult collides in name with AstrBot's
  CommandResult alias (= MessageEventResult). Keeping our own dataclass
  but documenting it, and never returning it from the handler.
- The handler let its own exceptions escape, so any bug became a raw
  traceback in the chat.
- Relying on decorator-injected *args is fragile: with a *args
  signature AstrBot cannot fill parsed params, so argv is now parsed
  from message_str directly.

New admin-only debug surface:
- /shit debug [target]  full gate breakdown, why nothing moved
- /shit tags [target]   dump taste vector terms
- /shit forceout        unconditional relay, ignores direction/taste/
                        confidence/LLM rerank
- /shit forcein         unconditional intake, updates taste, no send

Pipeline gains pending(), force_delivery() and run() (sync bridge for
the sync command layer). Commands takes optional probes instead of
importing the pipeline.

Tests: 47 (was 34), including a handler-level regression that proves an
exception becomes plain text, and a stubbed-astrbot loader so main.py
is actually exercised.
